00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:03.000
the problem is that the studies that
produce these ratings don't actually

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.890
reflect what happens when you use these
ingredients in skin care products for a

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:19.320
lot of reasons firstly the tests often
aren't done in real-world conditions in

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:24.090
an ideal world we test every single
product on every single person's face

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.650
and then we develop a really definitive
list of what will and won't break you

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.830
out
but this would be impossible it would

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.430
cost too much there's way too many
products to try and everyone's face and

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:39.390
getting a lot of people to use just one
product and not change their daily

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:44.550
routine for weeks or months at a time
this would just wouldn't happen instead

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:49.440
what's used in a scientific study is a
model a situation that mimics the

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.340
real-world situation but it's going to
be a lot simpler to carry out and

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.570
control and interpret there's lots of
examples of scientific models things

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.870
like crash test dummies samples of hair
that get dyed

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.430
pouring liquid onto sanitary pads patch
testing things on your arm

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:10.560
testing bikes on a racetrack most of the
time these models work pretty well but

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:15.420
usually they don't have everything that
would happen in real life so you can't

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:19.110
just apply their results really
straightforwardly to everyday life in

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:23.070
other words the external validity can be
questionable when we're talking about

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:33.900
comedogenicity ratings the models
aren't that great the most common tests

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.820
for comedogenicity is the rabbit ear
model this was pioneered in cosmetics

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:43.079
testing by two really famous
dermatologists Albert Kligman and James

00:03:43.079 --> 00:03:48.360
Fulton this happened in the 1970s what
the rabbit ear model was was you apply

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.750
the substance to the inner ear of a
rabbit and then you wait a few weeks and

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.920
see if you get any clogged pores or comedones 
rabbit ears are a lot more

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.030
sensitive than human skin so they
react to these ingredients much faster

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.390
which was really convenient
the problem is there's lots of false

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:08.910
positives so ingredients that aren't
comedogenic in humans would be in a

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.430
rabbit ear
in the original test there was another

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:16.049
problem rabbit ears have naturally
enlarged pores and some of the earlier

00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:19.680
results countered these bigger pores as
acne which meant there were even more

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.370
false positives so in other words there
were ingredients that people thought

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:27.810
were really comedogenic even though
it was just an experimental error the

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:32.400
most famous false positive is petroleum
jelly which is also known as petrolatum

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.840
the only ingredient in Vaseline this
false positive was corrected in the late

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:41.849
1980s but whether or not it was
comedogenic was debated until the mid

00:04:41.849 --> 00:04:46.889
1990s this wasn't the first time that
the rabbit ear model had problems there

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:50.550
were usually lots of conflicting results
and that's why lots of these comedogenic

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:53.070
ingredient lists disagree with each
other

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:58.770
more recently in 2007 two dermatologists
wrote the rabbit ear model is unable to

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:03.509
accurately depict the acnegenic
potential of chemical compounds and is

00:05:03.509 --> 00:05:07.530
therefore only valuable for
distinguishing absolute negatives in

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:11.340
other words the rabbit ear model can
only tell us about what things are

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:21.900
really really unlikely to cause clogged
pores if rabbit ears don't reflect what

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:26.940
happens on human skin then the obvious
solution is to try it on human skin but

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:32.669
again we got more problems firstly in
human skin tests they usually use the

00:05:32.669 --> 00:05:37.979
skin on people's backs the problem is
back skin is different from face skin so

00:05:37.979 --> 00:05:41.820
for example your face skin has a lot
more hair follicles and it's exposed to

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.389
a lot more sunlight that means that
whether your back and your face react the

00:05:45.389 --> 00:05:50.130
same way to ingredients is pretty
questionable human tests also use people

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:54.240
with large pores who are more prone to
getting pimples will someone with small

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.930
pores react the same way to these
ingredients most of the time the way

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:01.409
that these tests are conducted is that
the ingredient that's being tested is

00:06:01.409 --> 00:06:06.300
swabbed onto your skin and then they
cover it with a bandage this isn't

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.349
typically what you do with skin care if
you cover an ingredient what happens is

00:06:10.349 --> 00:06:14.009
you have greater penetration which means
that you're more likely to get pimples

00:06:14.009 --> 00:06:17.490
so think about things like when you have
clothing rubbing against your skin

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:22.710
this can cause pimples the human tests
also done a relatively small sample

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:28.169
usually it's less than 10 people and so
again there's the problem where it might

00:06:28.169 --> 00:06:32.340
not be so reliable you might not get the
same result if you test it on 10 other

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:36.360
people or on a hundred people or a
thousand people so again how useful

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.620
these ratings are whether we can apply
them in our everyday usage of skin care

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:50.639
products and cosmetics it's been pretty
overstated another huge issue with these

00:06:50.639 --> 00:06:55.800
comedogenic ingredients is that even if
an ingredient is comedogenic on its own

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:00.660
it might not be once you put it into a
product and even if a product doesn't

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:04.860
have any comedogenic ingredients it can
still cause pimples when you put it on

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:09.539
your skin there's a saying in biology
which is the dose makes the poison so

00:07:09.539 --> 00:07:13.500
for example if you breathe in humid air
it doesn't kill you and it's actually

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:18.090
quite nice but if you breathe in too
much water like in the ocean then you

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:22.470
drown drinking one glass of wine is
probably fine but 10 glasses will give

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:27.060
you a massive hangover 50 glasses will
probably kill you so how much you have

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:31.349
of an ingredient makes a huge difference
to your skin and clogged pores work this

00:07:31.349 --> 00:07:36.360
way as well here's the quote from a 1996
paper from Kligman substances that are

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:40.560
strongly comedogenic when tested
neat which means by itself or in high

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.570
concentrations become non comedogenic
after sufficient dilution for example in

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:51.240
a study published in 2006
100% pure acetylated lanolin alcohol

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:59.009
gave a really high comedogenic rating of
4 to 5 a 50% it was still 4 to 5 but

00:07:59.009 --> 00:08:04.830
when it was diluted to 25% it became a
rating of 1 most skin care products

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:08.520
contain lots and lots of different
ingredients and most of them are well

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:12.979
below 25% and if they're diluted by that
much they might not have the same effect

00:08:12.979 --> 00:08:19.110
so a typical face lotion moisturizer has
80% water which means that all of the

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:22.860
other ingredients will max out at 20%
and that's if you only have one other

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:27.030
ingredient in your product the same
study also found that products which had

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:30.860
notable comedogenic ingredients with 4
to 5 ratings things like cocoa butter

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:35.430
isopropyl palmitate and isopropyl isostearate
they didn't actually increase the

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.949
