00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:15.839
so what does all of this mean it means
that these comedogenicity scales are

00:10:15.839 --> 00:10:20.100
only useful in very limited
circumstances so the first case is

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:24.389
narrowing down what might be causing
your breakouts if you're breaking out

00:10:24.389 --> 00:10:27.929
and you're not sure which product is
causing it then checking for really

00:10:27.929 --> 00:10:32.490
comedogenic ingredients like four to
five ratings high up on an ingredients

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:36.990
list might help you look in the right
direction if you have a product and it

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:41.850
has no comedogenic ingredients then it's
less likely to be the culprit but it

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:45.509
could still be so it's important to
remember that this is only a starting

00:10:45.509 --> 00:10:49.470
point and it's not conclusive at all if
your skin is really sensitive to

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:52.610
clogging
then it might be worth avoiding products

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:56.780
with large amounts of comedogenic
ingredients if you're really acne prone

00:10:56.780 --> 00:11:00.500
